5:player
138:Island Adventure
139:The group from One Han City sets foot on the mysterious island alongside Frieren, the mage from another world.
140:Ichihime
141:So this is where the fog is coming from, nyaa? It looks completely normal so far, nyaa.
142:Quite peaceful and serene, actually.
143:Kaavi
144:No. I have a premonition that trouble brews beneath the surface.
145:Yuzu
146:Argh... As much as I hate agreeing with Kaavi, I can feel something off, too.
147:The fog right now is surging with life mana... It feels just like a monster breathing right down our necks!
148:Leia
149:There's more than one mana surge... each varying in strength.
150:Ms. Frieren, have you noticed anything?
151:Frieren
152:Yes. Though these mana signatures differ, they weave together into a single barrier covering the entire island.
153:Strangely enough, I feel I can cast magic here just as I usually do.
154:Let's take a closer look.
156:Nyaa?! I thought this was a deserted island! Who knew there'd be such a huge complex here, nyaa... Even if it's all run-down.
157:By the way, what's with all these weird markings on the walls and floor, nyaa?
158:A blessing, perhaps, or a curse... Either way, they are echoes of fate.
160:Isn't it obvious?! It has to be whoever's behind the fog!
161:This isn't just random scrawling. It reeks of ancient magic... and the rune layout is super creepy!
162:...Argh?
163:As they speak, something glimmers deep within the ancient ruins.
164:A scrying crystal ball? I've never seen one shaped quite like this... But one thing is certain: it is spewing out fog-infused mana.
165:Is this a magical item unique to your world?
166:Let me try to analyze it, too.
168:Be careful. Keep an eye out for bizarre magic.
170:Watch out for traps. There might be hidden mechanisms.
172:I'm actually quite strong.
173:With Frieren's assistance, we quickly decipher the spell formula inside the crystal ball.
174:It's a spell that only lifts when certain conditions are met.
175:The fog's magic is directly linked to the crystal ball. To dispel it, we must first determine what image the crystal is projecting.
176:Then, we need to gather the corresponding ingredients and use an alchemy circle to craft the key item for each crystal ball.
177:Only then will the crystal stop generating more enchanted fog.
178:It seems we'll be staying on this island a while longer.
179:Still, the ingredients are all scattered across the island. That, too, is a thread woven by fate.
180:In that case, let's get moving, nyaa! ...What do we need to do first, nyaa?
181:We witches will stay here and analyze the images in the crystal ball.
182:Then I'll head outside to search for materials, nyaa... What about you, Master?
184:Keep exploring the ruins.
187:Do you want to stay and study those squiggles, Master?
188:I don't get them at all... I'll leave you to it then, nyaa.
189:As I stare at the strange etchings, a sudden haze clouds my mind.
190:When I come to, I find myself in a completely unfamiliar space.
191:Where am I? How did I get here?
192:I search the stone walls and tiled floor for anything that might guide me, yet even my recent footsteps leave no trace.
193:???
194:...
195:The surrounding fog abruptly thickens, pulsing as if alive.
196:Who's there?
197:!
198:A translucent hand formed of mist silently materializes beside me and reaches out.
199:Oh no!
200:<color=#6CC2B6>Zoltraak!</color>
201:In the nick of time, a beam of magic pierces through, dispelling the entity.
202:Frieren stands at the far end of the passageway, appearing out of nowhere.
203:...Good, I made it in time.
204:This island is far trickier than it looks. It's best to tread carefully.
205:Thanks, Frieren.
206:Let's save the area ahead for another time.
207:Yep! Let's leave those squiggles to the pros, nyaa!
208:I don't understand them at all, so I'd rather look around outside with you, Master!
209:Following the deciphered directions, I begin my search for the target alongside Ichihime.
210:Look over there, Master! Is that what we need for the crystal ball, nyaa?
211:Oh! Great job, Ichihime!
212:Talk about a smooth search, just like a Riichi Ippatsu, nyaa!
213:The moment Ichihime extends her hand, the surrounding fog abruptly thickens.
214:A translucent hand formed of mist silently materializes beside her and reaches out.
215:Ichihime, watch out!
217:In the nick of time, a beam of magic pierces through, dispelling the entity.
218:Frieren stands behind us, appearing out of nowhere.
219:That was a close call.
220:Let's save the area ahead for another time.
221:Returning to the crystal ball with Frieren, we find Leia and the others have already prepared the magic circle.
222:Argh... Are these ingredients alright? They won't just blow up in our faces, will they?
224:&￥%*#!
225:As the magic circle glows, the fog takes physical form once more.
226:The monster's back, nyaa!
227:If you please, Ms. Frieren!
228:Got it. //n<size=50><color=#6CC2B6>Zoltraak!</color></size>
229:...
230:The fog has lifted a bit.
231:Not just here – I can feel the fog across the entire island beginning to thin.
232:Explore ruins, locate the crystal ball, break the spell... Argh, is it going to be like this the whole way?
233:It seems so... Our journey here looks set to take quite some time. Why don't we rest a bit before moving on?
234:Yes, tidying this place up to serve as our base of operations sounds like a fine idea.
235:However, before anyone can truly relax...
236:THUD!
237:What on earth is this blocky monster?! It's insanely strong!
238:That voice... Is it coming from farther down the corridor?
239:{var:player_nickname}, Ichihime, follow me.
240:Let's go investigate.
241:We approach closer to the source of the noise...
242:I'll provide cover, Mr. Stark.
243:Got it! Next strike goes here, right, Fern?
244:Monster
245:ROAR!
246:The mahjong tiles came alive and are attacking, nyaa?!
247:Fern
248:No matter how many times we knock it down, it keeps getting back up...
249:Stark
250:Isn't there any way to finish this thing off for good?!
251:This will turn into a war of attrition at this rate. Should I use a more powerful spell to blast it away all at once?
252:...No way! That'll collapse the whole corridor!
253:Looks like they need help.
254:{var:player_nickname}, can you spot the monster's weak point?
255:Even if you ask me that...
256:A monster made of mahjong tiles – its limbs form triplets and sequences, while its chest, back, and head each bear an identical tile.
257:Wait, fifteen tiles... four sets and a pair...
258:That's exactly one tile over a winning hand!
259:I've got it!
261:Hit it on the head!
263:Aim for the center!
264:Since there's one tile too many, all that's needed is to discard it!
265:BOOM!
266:A beam of magic strikes the weak point with pinpoint accuracy, obliterating the extra tile.
267:With that tile "discarded," the remaining tiles on the monster align perfectly into a winning hand.
268:The monster freezes, then dissolves into the thinning fog.
269:It worked... It's not getting back up.
270:Phew... That's finally over.
272:Ms. Frieren! What a relief to see you again.
273:Just as I sensed earlier, Frieren ended up here too... Ah, and who are you guys?
274:Were you the ones who helped us just now...?
275:That's a long story, nyaa...
279:With Frieren leading the way, we head toward the nearest source of mana.
282:Glad to see you two are unhurt, Fern, Stark.
283:Who'd actually live in a place like this and leave all this graffiti, nyaa?
286:Join the search for materials.
287:Oh no, nyaa!
288:The vision in the crystal ball matches... Now!
291:Don't worry, {var:player_nickname}.
